WEBVTT

00:10:29.541 --> 00:10:32.294
And our stories, our narratives,
are not just cognitive --

00:10:32.294 --> 00:10:34.004
they live in our bodies,

00:10:34.046 --> 00:10:36.548
and our bodies structure
and shape our stories.

00:10:37.174 --> 00:10:38.801
So knowing all this,

00:10:38.801 --> 00:10:41.637
recognizing the constructive
nature of it all,

00:10:41.679 --> 00:10:45.015
maybe we can hold on
less tightly to our stories.

00:10:45.599 --> 00:10:47.518
Maybe we can learn to let go.

00:10:49.103 --> 00:10:50.729
But that's easier said than done,

00:10:50.771 --> 00:10:53.107
because the thing
that is doing the letting go

00:10:53.107 --> 00:10:55.609
is also the thing
that has to be let go of.

00:10:55.651 --> 00:10:57.528
(Laughter)

00:10:58.946 --> 00:11:03.325
Maybe we can just marvel
at the efforts of people over millennia,